    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2024-june/q2",
      "question": "<p>With respect to the right-hand rule, a rotation through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta^\\circ\"></span> anticlockwise about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span>-axis is represented by the matrix</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix} \\cos \\theta &amp; -\\sin \\theta &amp; 0 \\\\ \\sin \\theta &amp; \\cos \\theta &amp; 0 \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Given that the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span>, where</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M = \\begin{pmatrix} -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} &amp; \\frac{1}{2} &amp; 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} &amp; -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} &amp; 0 \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>represents a rotation through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha^\\circ\"></span> anticlockwise about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span>-axis with respect to the right-hand rule,</p><p>(a) determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>(b) Hence determine the smallest possible positive integer value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> for which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M^k = \\mathbf I\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>The <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3 \\times 3\"></span> matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf N\"></span> represents a reflection in the plane with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = 0\"></span></p><p>(c) Write down the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf N\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2, 4, 3)\"></span></p><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> is the image of the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> under the transformation represented by matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span> followed by the transformation represented by matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf N\"></span>.</p><p>(d) Show that the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2 + \\sqrt{3}, 2\\sqrt{3} - 1, 3)\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> is the origin,</p><p>(e) show that, to 3 significant figures, the size of angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AOB\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"66.9^\\circ\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(f) Hence determine the area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AOB\"></span>, giving your answer to 3 significant figures.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
