    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2024-june/q3",
      "question": "<p>(a) Use the standard results for summations to show that, for all positive integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span>,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r^2(r+1) = \\frac{1}{12}n(n+1)(n+2)(an+b)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are integers to be determined.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(b) Hence show that, for all positive integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=k+1}^{3k} r^2(r+1) = \\frac{1}{3}k(3k+1)(Ak^2+Bk+C)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A, B\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> are integers to be determined.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>(c) Hence, using algebra and making your method clear, determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> for which</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"25\\sum_{r=k+1}^{3k} r^2(r+1) = 192k^3(3k+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
