    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2024-june/q4",
      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{A} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 &amp; -2 &amp; -7 \\\\ 3 &amp; k &amp; 2 \\\\ 1 &amp; 1 &amp; 4 \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{B} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4k - 2 &amp; 1 &amp; 7k - 4 \\\\ -10 &amp; 3 &amp; -19 \\\\ 3 - k &amp; -1 &amp; 6 - k \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>(a) Determine the value of the constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> for which</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{AB} = (3k + c)\\mathbf{I}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(b) Hence determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> for which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{A}^{-1}\"></span> does not exist.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{A}^{-1}\"></span> does exist,</p><p>(c) write down <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{A}^{-1}\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>(d) Use the answer to part (c) to solve the simultaneous equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-x - 2y - 7z = 10\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3x + ky + 2z = 3\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x + y + 4z = 1\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>giving the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x, y\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span> in simplest form in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
