    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2024-june/q5",
      "question": "<p>Given that on an Argand diagram the locus of points defined by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|z + 5 - 12i| = 10\"></span> is a circle,</p><p>(a) write down,</p><p>(i) the coordinates of the centre of this circle,</p><p>(ii) the radius of this circle.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(b) Show, by shading on an Argand diagram, the set of points defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"|z + 5 - 12i| \\leq 10\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>(c) For the set of points defined in part (b), determine the maximum value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|z|\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>The set of points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A = \\{ z : 0 \\leq \\arg(z + 5 - 20i) \\leq \\pi \\} \\cap \\{ z : |z + 5 - 12i| \\leq 10 \\}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>(d) Determine the area of the region defined by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, giving your answer to 3 significant figures.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
