      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:154mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8fm0-01-2024-june/q08-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figures 1 and 2. Central cross-section of the ornament and the shaded region R.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows the central vertical cross-section, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"OABCDEO\"></span>, of the design for a solid glass ornament.</p><p>Figure 2 shows the finite region, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, which is bounded by the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis, the horizontal line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"CB\"></span>, the vertical line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BA\"></span>, and the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AO\"></span>.</p><p>The ornament is formed by rotating the region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\"></span> about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis.</p><p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AO\"></span> is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x = ky^2 + \\sqrt{y} \\quad 0 \\leqslant y \\leqslant 4\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0.4, 4)\"></span> and the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0.4, 4.5)\"></span>.</p><p>The units are centimetres.</p><p>(a) Determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> according to this model.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(b) Use algebraic integration to determine the exact volume of glass that would be required to make the ornament, according to the model.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></p><p>(c) State a limitation of the model.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>When the ornament was manufactured, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9\\text{ cm}^3\"></span> of glass was required.</p><p>(d) Use this information and your answer to part (b) to evaluate the model, explaining your reasoning.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
